    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0215" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60F31/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Praha</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-04T12:00:00+01:00">March 4,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 4—10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Your instructions numbers 20, January 11 and 29, February 14.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d106-f1"/> The press now gives prominence to the report that you
                    intend to make public a list of those nations “which will not relinquish certain
                    import restrictions which the United States considers unjustified.” Foreign
                    Office official has intimated the concern of this Government lest it be included
                    therein and inquires whether it may be informed as to specific instances if any.
                    In view of results of representations, reported in my telegram 11, March 4, 11
                        a.m.,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d106-f2"/> I may be able to utilize <pb
                        facs="0216" n="140" xml:id="pg140"/> to advantage information of this nature
                    if such be your intention and have already mentioned difficulties with
                    automobiles, lard, and prunes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
